# Statement fixtures are byte-exact inputs to parsers and to import identity: a Parqet
# row's ID is a hash of the row, and OFX and PDF statements are parsed as given. Git must
# never apply text or line-ending normalization to them, or a test silently tests
# something else.
*.ofx  binary
*.qfx  binary
*.pdf  binary
# CSV stays diffable but is never normalized: CRLF in a bank or Parqet export is kept.
*.csv  -text
